=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: csw1
diagnosis_text:
The OSPF adjacency between CSW1 (10.0.0.34) and R1 (10.0.0.33) is failing because CSW1's eth0 interface — the CD_WAN_LINK_1 segment — was configured as an OSPF passive interface after the recent routine config change. This is confirmed directly by `show ip ospf interface eth0` on CSW1, which reports "No Hellos (Passive interface)" and shows "Multicast group memberships: <None>", meaning the interface has left the OSPF multicast groups and is neither sending nor accepting Hello packets. R1's eth0, by contrast, is fully active: it has joined OSPFAllRouters and OSPFDesignatedRouters multicast groups and is transmitting Hellos every 10 seconds — but CSW1 silently discards them, so the adjacency never progresses past initialization. The subnet (10.0.0.32/30) is still being advertised into OSPF area 0 from CSW1's side (the `network 10.0.0.32/30 area 0` statement remains), so the interface appears in the LSDB but carries no neighbor, which is why CSW1 shows 7 active interfaces but only 5 fully adjacent neighbors. Traffic continues via CSW2 because that WAN path is unaffected. The root cause is a single erroneous line added to CSW1's FRR config: `ip ospf passive` under `interface eth0`. The corrective fix is to remove that line from CSW1's interface eth0 stanza (in vtysh: `interface eth0` → `no ip ospf passive`), which will immediately allow Hellos to flow and the Full adjacency with R1 to reform.
=== END ===